  "grammar": [
    {
      "title": "Dative subjects: ମୋତେ ଭୋକ ଲାଗୁଛି",
      "body": "Feelings, needs and likes are often expressed with the person in the **dative** (to-me) form and the thing as the grammatical subject:\nମୋତେ ଭୋକ ଲାଗୁଛି — *to-me hunger is-striking* — 'I'm hungry'\nମୋତେ ମାଛ ଭଲ ଲାଗେ — *to-me fish good feels* — 'I like fish'\nମୋତେ ପାଣି ଦରକାର — *to-me water needed* — 'I need water'\n\nDative pronouns: **ମୋତେ** me · **ଆମକୁ** us · **ତୋତେ** you (intimate) · **ତୁମକୁ** you (familiar) · **ଆପଣଙ୍କୁ** you (formal) · **ତାକୁ** him/her · **ତାଙ୍କୁ** him/her (resp.) · **ସେମାନଙ୍କୁ** them. With nouns add **-କୁ** (*-ku*): ପିଲାକୁ 'to the child'.\n\nThe verb ଲାଗିବା stays the same whoever the person is: ଲାଗେ (generally), ଲାଗୁଛି (right now), ଲାଗିଲା (felt).",
      "examples": [
        { "native": "ମୋତେ ଶୋଷ ଲାଗୁଛି।", "roman": "mote sosô laguchhi.", "en": "I'm thirsty." },
        { "native": "ତୁମକୁ ଭୋକ ଲାଗୁଛି କି?", "roman": "tumôku bhokô laguchhi ki?", "en": "Are you hungry?" },
        { "native": "ତାଙ୍କୁ ରାଗ ଖାଇବା ଭଲ ଲାଗେ ନାହିଁ।", "roman": "taṅku ragô khaiba bhôlô lage nahiṃ.", "en": "He/She doesn't like spicy food." },
        { "native": "ଆମକୁ ଦୁଇଟି ଥାଳି ଦରକାର।", "roman": "amôku duiṭi thaḷi dôrôkarô.", "en": "We need two thalis." },
        { "native": "ଆପଣଙ୍କୁ ପଖାଳ ଭଲ ଲାଗିଲା?", "roman": "apôṇôṅku pôkhaḷô bhôlô lagila?", "en": "Did you like the pakhala?" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Want, love, and ordering",
      "body": "With an ordinary subject you can also say:\n**ମୁଁ … ଭଲ ପାଏ** — I love/really like … (ଆପଣ ଭଲ ପାଆନ୍ତି, ତୁମେ ଭଲ ପାଅ)\n**ମୁଁ … ଚାହେଁ** — I want … (polite, slightly formal)\n\nTo **order**, use a polite command: **ଦିଅନ୍ତୁ** 'please give', **ଆଣନ୍ତୁ** 'please bring'. To make it negative, add ନାହିଁ: ଦିଅନ୍ତୁ ନାହିଁ 'please don't give'.\n\nThe **future** tense is the polite way to offer: ଆପଣ କ'ଣ ଖାଇବେ? 'What will you eat?', ଚା ପିଇବେ? 'Will you have tea?'. Present negative: ମୁଁ ମାଂସ ଖାଏ ନାହିଁ (colloquially ଖାଏନି).",
      "examples": [
        { "native": "ମୁଁ ପଖାଳ ଭଲ ପାଏ।", "roman": "muṃ pôkhaḷô bhôlô pae.", "en": "I love pakhala." },
        { "native": "ମୁଁ ଗୋଟିଏ କପ୍ ଚା ଚାହେଁ।", "roman": "muṃ goṭie kôp cha chaheṃ.", "en": "I'd like a cup of tea." },
        { "native": "ଦୁଇ ପ୍ଲେଟ୍ ଭାତ ଆଣନ୍ତୁ।", "roman": "dui pleṭ bhatô aṇôntu.", "en": "Bring two plates of rice, please." },
        { "native": "ଚା ପିଇବେ?", "roman": "cha piibe?", "en": "Will you have some tea?" },
        { "native": "ମୁଁ ମାଂସ ଖାଏ ନାହିଁ।", "roman": "muṃ maṅsô khae nahiṃ.", "en": "I don't eat meat." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "dialogue": {
